-- #56 알림 수신 설정 (ADR-0162; N05 §4·§8, owner answers 56-1…56-3 and #52's 52-21·52-22·52-23 of
-- 2026-11-21). Generated by `drizzle-kit generate`, then hand-edited where marked: this header and
-- the tail. The snapshot is as generated. Additive: one column with a constant default, its CHECK
-- and a privilege narrowing; no existing row changes, so no reset (docs/RESET.md).
--
-- - notification_inboxes.categories_off: the categories the member turned off, an opt-out list —
--   '{}' (the default: no row rewritten, no backfill) is every category on (52-21 '처음엔 켜짐').
--   The write path's gate reads it in the statement and lock it already takes (FOR KEY SHARE SKIP
--   LOCKED) and skips an input of an off category (52-22: nothing is made while off); what the
--   inbox holds stays (56-1). It goes with the inbox at the closure, as the notifications do.
-- - notification_inboxes_categories_off_check: categories of NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES only (the
--   three of 52-21, generated from the shared list as `notifications_category_check` is); `<@`
--   also refuses a NULL element. A fourth category regenerates both CHECKs in its own migration.
-- - Both ALTERs take ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on the inboxes: they wait for the notification writers in
--   flight and the writers arriving meanwhile wait for them — a brief stall, nothing fails.
-- - No enum, event type, admin action type or release setting value.
ALTER TABLE "notification_inboxes" ADD COLUMN "categories_off" text[] DEFAULT '{}'::text[] NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "notification_inboxes" ADD CONSTRAINT "notification_inboxes_categories_off_check" CHECK ("notification_inboxes"."categories_off" <@ ARRAY['trade', 'market', 'community']::text[]);--> statement-breakpoint
-- Hand-edited: of an inbox buddha_app now changes the member's 수신 설정 only. It keeps SELECT,
-- INSERT and DELETE (the trigger's insert, the closure's delete) and UPDATE of `categories_off` —
-- enough for the row locks the writers (FOR KEY SHARE) and the closure (FOR UPDATE) take, which
-- need UPDATE privilege on some column. No update of `user_id` (a key update, which the writers'
-- gate would skip as `no_inbox`, and a way round the insert-only guards that keep an inbox off
